# A bad month that starts with a multi-byte character is underlined whole, never half of it.
mode: syntax
---- query
datetime(2024-é1-01)
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..22
  PIPELINE@0..21
    LITERAL@0..21
      DATETIME@0..21 "datetime(2024-é1-01)"
  WHITESPACE@21..22 "\n"

error[DS0003]: invalid datetime `2024-é1-01`
  --> query:1:15
  |
1 | datetime(2024-é1-01)
  |               ^ expected a month (1 or 2 digits)
  |
  = help: write an ISO 8601 date: `datetime(2024-01-31)` or `datetime(2024-01-31T12:00:00Z)`
